# libclc
### The OpenCL C library of LLVM, what Mesa needs for rusticl. Since LLVM 23 it is a runtime built
### with the just built clang, which the cross build of lfs/llvm cannot run: the SPIR-V it produces
### is target independent, so it is built here with the native clang of the global toolchain and
### the llvm-spirv of the cross translator (postbuild.sh)
PKG_VER=${LLVM_VER}
### No PKG_URL: the sources are the ones lfs/llvm extracted, used in place
PKG_SRCDIR=llvm_${PKG_VER}
PKG_DEPS="lfs/llvm lfs/Vulkan-SPIRV-LLVM-Translator:cross"
BUILD_PROCESS=none
